# Generated Gaussian splat binaries.
# Captures are large and regenerable; real surveys belong in release assets or
# an external bucket, per the $0 bandwidth rule in CLAUDE.md. Regenerate the
# synthetic stand-in with:
#   python3 scripts/cleanup_splat.py --synthesize <path>
*.splat
*.ply
models/sam2/

# Downloaded GDTF fixture profiles.
# Archives run to tens of megabytes each and are redistributable only under
# GDTF Share's terms, so the cache is a local artifact rather than repository
# content. Repopulate it with:
#   GDTF_SHARE_USER=... GDTF_SHARE_PASSWORD=... npm run fetch:gdtf
public/assets/fixtures/cache/
*.gdtf

# Fetched open-data venue layers (terrain grid, NAIP orthoimagery, OSM
# vectors) for showcase/open-data-venue.html. About 1.2 MB per venue and
# fully regenerable from public sources, so a local artifact per CLAUDE.md
# §11. Repopulate with:
#   npm run fetch:open-data
public/assets/scans/open_data/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# Local environment files and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
test-results/

# Unreal generated files and local build evidence
native/**/Binaries/
native/**/Intermediate/
native/**/Saved/
native/**/DerivedDataCache/
native/**/.vs/
native/**/Build/Windows/
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb

# Local $0 AI memory (ChromaDB vector store + NetworkX import graph pickle).
# Regenerated by `python scripts/memory/ingest.py`; the ONNX embedder auto-
# downloads on first ingest (~80 MB, into %USERPROFILE%\.cache\chroma). Not
# committed per CLAUDE.md §11 — see §14 for stack details.
.memory/
.agents/memory/

# Packaging artifacts
installation-bundle/
installer-build/
*.zip
*.exe
*.obj
SpatialPrevis-Linux-Installer.sh

# Generated prompt-template drafts from scripts/ai-tools/metaprompt.py.
# Per-workstation output, analogous to .memory/ above -- the tool itself and
# its curated examples/ are committed, these task-specific run artifacts are
# not.
scripts/ai-tools/prompts/
